rows.before:
You'll go back for it?
Yes, I think that's much better.
Better than giving up on your homework, at least...{p}

rows.en:
You'd go back for it?
Yes, I think that's much better.
Better than giving up on your homework, at least...{p}

rows.before:
That's awful...
A girl staying alone? That's dangerous!
...That's what they were all saying, and yet.{p}

rows.en:
That's cruel...
"It's dangerous to leave a girl alone!"
...That's what they were all saying, and yet.{p}

rows.before:
Then on Monday, friends would trade information: which places they'd searched, whether they'd found anything like a clue, "I saw something like a child's ghost," that sort of thing.
A stupid game.
Quite a lot of them exaggerated, or twisted things to fit, too.{p}

rows.en:
Then on Monday, friends would trade information: which places they'd searched, whether they'd found anything like a clue, "I saw something like a child's ghost," that sort of thing.
A stupid game.
Quite a lot of them exaggerated, too, or made far-fetched connections.{p}

rows.before:
Nao was shut inside that same classroom once again.
Would this go on forever?
As he sank into despair, the child started saying this.{p}

rows.en:
Nao was shut inside that same classroom once again.
Would this go on forever?
As he sank into despair, the child began to speak.{p}

rows.before:
...Nao couldn't get out of that classroom in the old school building, again.
This time it was even more miserable.
He had fallen into the hole in the floor, so his chances of being found were even slimmer.{p}

rows.en:
...Once again, Nao couldn't get out of that classroom in the old school building.
This time it was even more miserable.
He had fallen into the hole in the floor, so his chances of being found were even slimmer.{p}

rows.before:
Then the boy grabbed Nao by the hair as hard as it could.
"I know. How about I make sure you can never run away again?"
And with that, his fate was sealed.{p}

rows.en:
Then the child grabbed Nao by the hair as hard as it could.
"I know. How about I make sure you can never run away again?"
And with that, his fate was sealed.{p}

rows.before:
Unable to bear the shock of his death, I finally took to my bed.
A high fever went on for days.
What came to my fever-tormented mind was a dream of Yuya.{p}

rows.en:
Unable to bear the shock of his death, I finally took to my bed.
A high fever went on for days.
In my fever-tormented mind, I dreamed of Yuya.{p}

rows.before:
Scary...?
Why...?
He keeps me bound to him only because he loves me that much.{p}

rows.en:
Scary...?
Why...?
He keeps me bound to him because he loves me that much.{p}

rows.before:
That boy who said he liked me... he died, all of a sudden.
On the train tracks, in the middle of the night...
...They wrote it off as suicide, but I just can't accept that.{p}

rows.en:
That boy who said he liked me... he died, all of a sudden.
On the railroad tracks, in the dead of night...
...They wrote it off as suicide, but I just can't accept that.{p}

rows.before:
Listen, spirit rapping.
Yuya is angry.
He's watching everything from behind me, you know...{p}

rows.en:
Hear that? It's spirit rapping.
Yuya is angry.
He's watching everything from behind me, you know...{p}

rows.before:
In an instant, the air in the room went tight as a wire.
Every eye turned to the door at once.
As we stared at it, it came again...{p}

rows.en:
In an instant, the air in the room went tight as a wire.
Every eye turned to the door at once.
As we stared at it, the knocking came again...{p}

rows.before:
It bugged me that the victims were all girls, but even so, I just couldn't see Shimada or the other boys in class being the thief...
And besides...
Something weird a friend of mine said was bugging me.{p}

rows.en:
It bugged me that the victims were all girls, but even so, I just couldn't see Shimada or the other boys in class being the thief...
And besides...
Something weird a friend of mine said was on my mind.{p}

rows.before:
Hmm, so you get it?
Well, Kawahara gradually started to find that kind of thing painful.
He'd smile and smile at his teachers and friends, while sticking his tongue out at them inside.{p}

rows.en:
Hmm, so you get it?
Well, Kawahara gradually started to find that kind of thing painful.
He'd be all smiles with his teachers and friends, while sticking his tongue out at them on the inside.{p}

rows.before:
"Me too!
I want some too...☆"
No sooner had Hosoda shouted than he tried to forcibly snatch the cup out of my hands.{p}

rows.en:
"Me too!
I want some too...☆"
No sooner had Hosoda shouted than he tried to snatch the cup right out of my hands.{p}

rows.before:
Back then...
Hosoda was in the way, so we just left the broken cup there and went home.
That tea... most of it spilled, but a little might have been left on the shards.{p}

rows.en:
Back then...
Hosoda was being such a nuisance that we just left the broken cup there and went home.
That tea... most of it spilled, but a little might have been left on the shards.{p}

rows.before:
...Behind her as she said it, a teacher I'd never seen before appeared.
"Hashimoto, what are you doing?
You were supposed to report to the reflection room today."{p}

rows.en:
...As she said it, a teacher I'd never seen before appeared behind her.
"Hashimoto, what are you doing?
You were supposed to report to the reflection room today."{p}

rows.before:
It was too dark to see clearly, but inside the shoe locker were a pair of eyes, dried out completely.
Not just eyes.
Clean-cut eyebrows, a shapely nose, purple lips...{p}

rows.en:
It was too dark to see clearly, but inside the shoe locker was a pair of eyes, completely dried out.
Not just eyes.
Clean-cut eyebrows, a shapely nose, purple lips...{p}

rows.before:
What had Kawahara wanted me to help him with?
Hashimoto had been so terribly depressed. Maybe he wanted me to be there for her...
He was called a two-faced person, but maybe deep down he was a good person after all.{p}

rows.en:
What had Kawahara wanted me to help him with?
Hashimoto had been so terribly depressed. Maybe he wanted me to be there for her...
People called him two-faced, but maybe deep down he was a good person after all.{p}
